<title>INDIA: India Reliance board meets after AGM.</title>
<headline>India Reliance board meets after AGM.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Reliance Industries Ltd's board will meet to finalise a bonus equity issue shortly after the firm's annual general meeting on Thursday, its chairman told shareholders.  </p>
<p>&quot;We will put curtain down, meet and discuss for 10-20 minutes and then come back and announce the ratio recommended by your board,&quot; Dhirubhai Ambani said at the start of the annual general meeting (AGM).</p>
<p>&quot;I hope you would support me in this approach.&quot;</p>
<p>Traders have said they expected the company to announce a bonus ratio of three shares for every five shares held -- the same ratio as the firm's last two bonus issues in the 1980s.</p>
<p>-- Bombay equities desk +91-22-265 9000</p>
